WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.141 --> 00:00:06.216
Newton’s third law is brutally simple: to every action, there is an equal and opposite

2
00:00:06.266 --> 00:00:11.341
reaction. A cold-gas thruster releases pressurized gas through a nozzle.

3
00:00:11.416 --> 00:00:18.076
As the gas accelerates outward, the vehicle experiences a force in the opposite

4
00:00:18.126 --> 00:00:18.734
direction.

5
00:00:19.259 --> 00:00:25.099
Arrange multiple nozzles at different positions, and forces can also create torque,

6
00:00:25.174 --> 00:00:31.894
changing pitch, roll, or yaw. But the supply of compressed gas is finite.

7
00:00:31.994 --> 00:00:36.294
Powerful bursts are not the same as unlimited endurance.

8
00:00:36.394 --> 00:00:40.769
A cold-gas thruster releases pressurized gas through a nozzle.

9
00:00:41.186 --> 00:00:46.811
The escaping gas carries momentum, so the remaining vehicle experiences a reaction

10
00:00:46.886 --> 00:00:53.461
force. A simple approximation for momentum thrust is mass flow rate times exhaust

11
00:00:53.536 --> 00:00:58.611
speed; a fuller model includes pressure across the exit area.

12
00:00:58.686 --> 00:01:01.365
The gas need not burn to push the vehicle.

13
00:01:01.777 --> 00:01:05.727
A force through the center of mass changes translation.

14
00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:10.882
The same force applied at a distance can also rotate the vehicle.

15
00:01:10.982 --> 00:01:16.169
Carefully distributed thrusters may generate pitch, roll and yaw moments.

16
00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:22.945
That introduces real control complexity, because translation and rotation can interact

17
00:01:22.995 --> 00:01:27.170
while the center of mass and vehicle orientation are changing.

18
00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:33.595
Gas tanks must store sufficient mass at safe pressure, survive structural loads and

19
00:01:33.695 --> 00:01:37.863
fit inside a vehicle already carrying batteries and passengers.

20
00:01:38.478 --> 00:01:44.653
Each maneuver consumes propellant. Unlike a continuously energized rotor system,

21
00:01:44.763 --> 00:01:50.188
stored gas provides finite reaction mass, and replenishment matters.

22
00:01:50.263 --> 00:01:54.884
An airborne stunt therefore says little about everyday flight endurance.
